 "answer_verbatim": "There isn’t a single objectively “best” roofer, but **T&S Roofing Systems** looks like a strong Miami candidate based on the available information: it reports a **4.8-star rating across 1,271+ reviews**, a **GAF Master Elite** certification, and Florida roofing license **CCC1326032**. Those are useful signals, not a guarantee of workmanship or a current license status.\n\nFor a hurricane-rated replacement, get at least three written bids and ask each contractor to specify the **Miami-Dade Notice of Acceptance (NOA) or other HVHZ approval for every roof component**—covering, underlayment, and fastening system—as well as the permit, inspection process, and workmanship warranty. Verify the contractor’s active license and insurance independently before signing.",
